From 0f9d1155971607488e33367625c55b66d2c18aef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:37:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ROCmFPX on Vulkan: the shader half, ported. NOT YET WORKING -
 it segfaults in execution.

Our fork has never had ROCmFPX on any GPU backend. CHECKED before this commit: a grep for rocmfp under ggml/src/ggml-vulkan was EMPTY on every branch we own, so the ROCmFP4/ROCmFPX weight formats were CPU-only here. charlie12345/ROCmFPX has carried Vulkan pipelines for FP2/FP3/FP4/FP4_FAST/FP6/FP8 the whole time. That is not a regression, it is work nobody did.

WHAT IS IN:
- 6 dequant shaders copied verbatim from rocmfpx/HEAD: rocmfp4, rocmfp4_fast, rocmfpx_fp2, fp3, fp6, fp8.
- types.glsl: their block structs, DATA_A_* selectors and the ROCMFPX_FAMILY predicate.
- dequant_funcs.glsl: 9 dequantize()/dequantize4() blocks lifted verbatim.
- dequant_funcs_cm2.glsl: 6 coopmat2 decode functions, plus the dequantFuncA binding chain, which lives apart from the bodies in upstream layout and had to be written.
- vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp: the 6 type names registered so the generator emits them.
- ggml-vulkan.cpp: our own Q2_0_G128 wiring mirrored across all 6 ROCmFP types - dequant, get_rows, mat-vec pipelines, and the type recognition switches. Mirroring our own precedent beats hand-porting their 412 lines against a backend 10,450 commits newer than theirs.

THE TRAP, and it would have been silent: ROCmFPX UE4M3 scale is NOT NVFP4 UE4M3. ROCmFPX decodes with exponent bias 119 and subnormal step 1/1024; NVFP4 uses 120 and 1/512. That is a factor of two on every scale. One shared lookup table would have doubled or halved every weight with no error anywhere. They get their own table.

DELIBERATE EXCLUSIONS, both because the shader does not exist rather than because we chose less:
- copy-to-quant. There is no GPU quantizer for these formats in their tree either. Decoding is the point.
- the q8_1 integer-dot mat-vec variants. Their own generator excludes ROCmFP from q8_1.

BUILD: green. 348 ROCmFP SPIR-V variants compiled in; the CLI binary grew 94.6 to 99.2 MB.

WHAT WORKS: the backend is intact. CHECKED - the new binary runs qwen2.5-0.5b-TQ4_1S fully on the 780M at 158.9 t/s prefill, 39.7 t/s generation.

WHAT DOES NOT: the ROCmFP4 Ornith 9B file SEGFAULTS during execution when fully offloaded. It used to abort at GGML_ASSERT(dmmv != nullptr) in pipeline lookup; the mat-vec pipelines are wired now and it gets past that, which is progress and nothing more. The crash is undiagnosed. Committed anyway so the port is durable and the next step starts from evidence, not from memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Conflict-resolved: S2: this commit's ROCmFP case labels went into the old mat-mat and mat-mat-id getter switches, which upstream 91f6a6cf3 removed (pipeline map; absent pipeline = nullptr = dequant+f16 fallback, the outcome 4c5b247b8 later forced by hand); nothing to carry
